<!--
  BlockML VS Code — documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.vscode.documentation.V2Scope
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:contrib="org.blockml.bml.vscode.contribution"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.vscode.documentation"
  xmlns:vtype="org.blockml.bml.vscode.type">

  <name>V2Scope</name>
  <type>doc:V2Scope</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to VS Code plugin V2 features</is>

  <documentation>
    V2 (milestone ReleaseMilestone::V2) — IDE-grade BML support on top of V1:

    1. Language Server integration — vscode-languageclient wiring to a BlockML LSP for diagnostics,
       hover, completion, and related capabilities declared on LanguageServerContribution.
    2. Advanced syntax highlighting — semantic tokens classified by FrameworkRoles position
       (same tag name, different color by nesting). The client runs the @blockml/lsp classifier
       locally so nested files keep coloring without the TextMate rule-stack limit; the language
       server still advertises the legend. TextMate remains a lexical fallback.
       semanticTokenScopes map legend types onto the existing *.bml scopes; colors are applied
       via editor.semanticTokenColorCustomizations (overlaySemanticTokenColors), not via
       tokenColorCustomizations alone (SemanticHighlightingContribution + GrammarContribution).
    3. Navigation between BML files — Ctrl/Cmd-click and shortcuts (go to definition, peek,
       find references) for Block types, baseType, properties, aggregations, associations,
       capabilities, see targets, instance ids, and xmlns prefixes — analogous to Java
       class/field navigation (NavigationContribution + Command/Keybinding contributions).

    V2 contributions are authored with milestone V2 and may remain enabled=false until the
    language server is ready; generators honour both flags.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="doc:GenerationWorkflow" relation="SeeAlso">
      How V2 slices are filtered during generation.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:LanguageServerContribution" relation="Defines">
      Language server client contribution.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:SemanticHighlightingContribution" relation="Defines">
      Advanced / semantic highlighting.
    </see>
    <see type="contrib:NavigationContribution" relation="Defines">
      Cross-file navigation feature.
    </see>
    <see type="vtype:NavigationKind" relation="SeeAlso">
      Navigable symbol kinds.
    </see>
    <see type="doc:V1Scope" relation="SeeAlso">
      V1 baseline that V2 builds on.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
